    {
      "id": "_1GUHhn255_rWrBEbfw5G",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 811.4395474159041,
      "y": 4039.6978110673517,
      "width": 1199,
      "height": 1050,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1838391303,
      "version": 2383,
      "versionNonce": 1687446606,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785380844552,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1 building brain -> that can understand text\n                    that can generate text based on input\n\n\nwe have LLM alreay in market, we can use this LLM, now a days it is not a big deal, before brain now we can\nchange our brain to LLM.\n\n\n2 -> If we want to use LLM as our brain, hence we need to put LLM in our system somewhere, Since LLMs are\n    very heavy deep learning models, which are trained on whole internet data, putting this is also a \n    challenge for computation and cost.\n    This problem is solved by companies already like OpenAI, Anthropic,Google which has made their LLM, \n    they have identified this problem, they have put these LLMs on their own servers, and they created APIs\n    around LLM. Using this API, anyone can talk to these LLMs. Hence we need to just hit APIs, no need to put\n    LLM in our server or system, and benefit of this we will pay acc to our usecase,jitna API use krenge utna\n    pay krenge, this is also a benefit for us.\n\n3 -> Orchestration of this whole system, all these components combinally running is also a challenge\n    we have multiple components in this system\n    1  AWS S3\n    2  Text Splitters\n    3  Embedding\n    4  Database\n    5  LLM\n    \n    these are the components, and we need to perform multiple tasks in pipeline\n    1 Document Loader\n    2 Text Splitter\n    3 Embedding\n    4 Database Management\n    5 Retreival task\n    6 LLM talk task\n\nIf we will write this whole code from scratch it could be very very difficult, lets say we have build\nthis system , and tomorrow we need to change our LLM as OpenAI is costly, we need to use Google Gemini\nor we need to use GCP in place of AWS or we need to use some other embedding models, here there are \nmany moving components, all this coding very very challenging,\nThis is where LangChain comes into the picture.\n\nLangchaing Gives builtin functionalities, where we can interacte with all these components. Not only\nthat, if tommorrow we want to use Google Gemini instead of OpenAI, no problem we can do that just\ndoing 1-2 line of change.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1 building brain -> that can understand text\n                    that can generate text based on input\n\n\nwe have LLM alreay in market, we can use this LLM, now a days it is not a big deal, before brain now we can\nchange our brain to LLM.\n\n\n2 -> If we want to use LLM as our brain, hence we need to put LLM in our system somewhere, Since LLMs are\n    very heavy deep learning models, which are trained on whole internet data, putting this is also a \n    challenge for computation and cost.\n    This problem is solved by companies already like OpenAI, Anthropic,Google which has made their LLM, \n    they have identified this problem, they have put these LLMs on their own servers, and they created APIs\n    around LLM. Using this API, anyone can talk to these LLMs. Hence we need to just hit APIs, no need to put\n    LLM in our server or system, and benefit of this we will pay acc to our usecase,jitna API use krenge utna\n    pay krenge, this is also a benefit for us.\n\n3 -> Orchestration of this whole system, all these components combinally running is also a challenge\n    we have multiple components in this system\n    1  AWS S3\n    2  Text Splitters\n    3  Embedding\n    4  Database\n    5  LLM\n    \n    these are the components, and we need to perform multiple tasks in pipeline\n    1 Document Loader\n    2 Text Splitter\n    3 Embedding\n    4 Database Management\n    5 Retreival task\n    6 LLM talk task\n\nIf we will write this whole code from scratch it could be very very difficult, lets say we have build\nthis system , and tomorrow we need to change our LLM as OpenAI is costly, we need to use Google Gemini\nor we need to use GCP in place of AWS or we need to use some other embedding models, here there are \nmany moving components, all this coding very very challenging,\nThis is where LangChain comes into the picture.\n\nLangchaing Gives builtin functionalities, where we can interacte with all these components. Not only\nthat, if tommorrow we want to use Google Gemini instead of OpenAI, no problem we can do that just\ndoing 1-2 line of change.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fT87FA1cEz1DpGtsnw1Jj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2467.091891165904,
      "y": 3492.3462485673517,
      "width": 275,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1365092585,
